This repository hosts two related projects on extreme-low-bit LLM
compression:

  1. BCJR-QAT --- a differentiable relaxation of trellis-coded weight
     quantization (this paper, Apr 2026).
  2. qtip-olmoe --- 2-bit weight-only PTQ for OLMoE-1B-7B with per-expert
     routing-conditioned Hessian calibration (prior work, used as the
     PTQ baseline in the BCJR-QAT paper).

Algorithmic attribution
-----------------------

The trellis-coded quantization algorithms (Viterbi encoder, BlockLDLQ
Hessian-aware rounding, HYB computed-Gaussian trellis, incoherence
processing) follow QTIP (Tseng et al., NeurIPS 2024).

    QTIP paper:   https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.11235
    QTIP code:    https://github.com/Cornell-RelaxML/qtip (GPL-3.0)

The BCJR forward-backward (sum-product) algorithm used in the
training-time relaxation follows Bahl, Cocke, Jelinek, Raviv (1974);
the algorithm is also a direct instance of the transfer-matrix
computation for 1D spin chains used in statistical mechanics.

    BCJR paper:   https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1974.1055186

The code under src/ (BCJR kernel, codebooks, Viterbi encoder,
BlockLDLQ, CUDA/Triton kernels, OLMoE and Llama adapters, QAT
pipeline, calibration pipeline, evaluation harness) is an independent
clean-room implementation of the algorithms described in the QTIP and
BCJR papers. No source code from the upstream QTIP repository is used,
linked, or redistributed here; the GPL-3.0 license of the upstream
QTIP project therefore does not transitively apply to this work.

